    "body": "FWIW I could go either way. We already divide form-associated elements up into several subcategories, and adding a new one called \"Autocapitalizable elements\" (or something more generic?) would be reasonable; trying to specify autocapitalization for img and object doesn't make a lot of sense. Note that \"listed elements\" = \"form-associated elements\" minus `img`, so that gets us a bit closer at least.\r\n\r\nOn the other hand, not inventing a new category just for this sounds kind of nice as well.",
