    "updated_at": "2018-01-22T21:32:04Z",
    "body": "I guess the more I stare at it, the more I think just using form-associated elements is the \"conceptually cleanest\" approach: we have decided that part of the computation of the `el.autocapitalize` IDL attribute is to consult the form owner, and it makes sense to do that for all elements that have a form owner, i.e. all form-associated elements.\r\n\r\nBut, I can understand the desire for shortest-path-to-interop. In that case we can just update the patch with a new category (\"form-associated autocapitalizable elements\", I suppose).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/359571892/reactions",
